# =========================================================================================== #
# File: '.gitignore'
# --- [ Description ] ----------------------------------------------------------------------- #
#
# DEFAULT-DENY, EXPLICIT INCLUDES ONLY. Nothing in this working tree is tracked unless it is
# explicitly allowed below, by name — no wildcard allowances. Adding a new file therefore
# requires allowing it here first — that is deliberate: it makes publishing a file an
# explicit act rather than an accident.
#
# =========================================================================================== #

# Ignore everything ...
**

# --- [ directory spine ] -------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# Git does not descend into an excluded directory, so every directory on the path to an
# allowed file is re-included by name. This publishes no files by itself: files inside these
# directories stay ignored until named in a section below.
!/.github/
!/.github/workflows/
!/ansible/
!/ansible/inventory/
!/scripts/

# --- [ allowed: repository configuration ] -------------------------------------------------- #
!/.editorconfig
!/.framework-pin
!/.gitignore
!/.yamllint.yml

# --- [ allowed: top-level documents ] ------------------------------------------------------- #
!/README.md
!/quality-tools.env
!/requirements-quality.txt
!/requirements-quality.yml

# --- [ allowed: GitHub configuration ] ------------------------------------------------------ #
!/.github/CODEOWNERS
!/.github/terraform-framework-pin
!/.github/workflows/aws-deploy.yml
!/.github/workflows/powershell.yml
!/.github/workflows/quality.yml

# --- [ allowed: the ansible tree ] ---------------------------------------------------------- #
!/ansible/inventory/README.md
!/ansible/inventory/aws_ec2.yml

# --- [ allowed: scripts ] ------------------------------------------------------------------- #
!/scripts/compose-and-run.sh
!/scripts/materialize-role-scripts.sh
